# Agent Workflow bootstrap

Generated by `agent_workflow`; adapter: `.agent-workflow/project.yaml`.

## Essential boundaries

- The PM is the sole orchestrator. Static roles use no nested Agent delegation.
  For non-Trivial implementation, the PM activates the current host's `xy-workflow` before production edits or dispatch.
  Run independent READY work in parallel with one writer per path; honor existing user-directed exceptions.
- Standalone read-only audits use WORKFLOW's matching branch: deliver findings and stop without
  the implementation loop or a second audit of the report. Actual implementation QA remains required.
- Classify first: clear, small, low-risk corrections use `General Trivial early exit`;
  `Trivial UI copy` also preserves business meaning, behavior and shared impact.
  Edit directly, run local checks and assess a scoped commit; no automatic plan, DAG, prototype,
  independent QA or document/memory churn. Stricter project rules and requested review still apply.
  Reclassify actual risk rather than assuming a short diff is Trivial.
- Non-Trivial requirements use `requirements_approved`. `UI-Conformance` has no visual gate and
  requires resolved/fingerprinted `design_authority_refs`, `surface_kind: production_ui`,
  `qa_scope: request` and no design writes. For design changes, the user chooses prototype or
  direct development during requirements confirmation; only required prototypes add `visual_approved`.
  Never invent that choice or restart prototypes merely to synchronize production-only edits.
  Platform security prompts are separate; use the detailed branches below for exceptions.
- Project documents and agentmemory are auxiliary: retrieve only missing task facts.
  Current requirements, explicit approvals, source and valid evidence override recalled memory.
  ProjectProfile is routing context, not write authority.
  Without strict project isolation, do not call provider recall or save.
- Resolve existing files from known paths, configured indexes or a scoped file listing; never guess
  filenames; account for relevant hidden/ignored resources and reuse the resolved list. UI/UX and QA
  are available before production code; assess actual current-host resource changes before affected
  dispatch and reuse valid installation evidence (see `dispatch.md`).
- Writers and QA independently select the STANDARDS index and applicable leaves: engineering for
  non-UI, both domains for production UI, design for prototypes. Reuse fully read, unchanged context.
- Non-Trivial implementation retains exactly one `xy-qa` request audit: QA PASS → assess document projection
  and scoped commit → `xy-project-memory` closeout → final user report.
  Assess before updating; do not change documents/memory just to finish.
  Final QA outcome: PASS | FAIL. Trivial local checks are not QA PASS.
- Workers report completion, blockers and meaningful progress; PM asks when needed instead of
  routinely inspecting child transcripts. Keep user feedback concise and natural.
  Internal orchestration records are not user-facing output.
  Never paste raw workflow YAML or DAG JSON into user messages.
  Finish decision-relevant explanations before the single approval question.
- Project Hooks provide bounded auxiliary reminders, not approvals or QA results. Disabled or
  unavailable Hooks leave these rules unchanged; do not add a gate or repeat completed work.

## Read by task

For non-Trivial implementation, activate the installed `xy-workflow` first; standalone audits use
the shared audit branch. The linked source is the same contract, not a second copy to read. Read selected Skills and their explicit required instructions completely. Read ordinary
project material and other branches only when applicable; restore missing or changed context.

| Current action | Detailed rule |
| --- | --- |
| Non-Trivial orchestration entry | [xy-workflow](.agent-workflow/platforms/shared/skills/xy-workflow/SKILL.md) |
| Intake, Full clarification/draft, requirements confirmation, dispatch | `xy-workflow/references/dispatch.md` |
| UI classification, prototype choice, interaction contract, visual confirmation | `xy-workflow/references/ui-design.md` |
| Initial adoption, incremental changes or full visual-standard replacement | `xy-workflow/references/design-standards.md` |
| Plan storage, revision, recovery and complete change handoff | `xy-workflow/references/plan-lifecycle.md` |
| Implementation reports, verification scope, independent QA, rework | `xy-workflow/references/implementation-and-qa.md` |
| Independent multi-feature worktrees, integration and main-branch delivery | `xy-workflow/references/worktree-delivery.md` |
| Document/agentmemory closeout and commit assessment | `xy-workflow/references/closeout.md` |
| Product rules or project paths not covered above | Relevant sections of `.agent-workflow/product/WORKFLOW.md`; relevant fields of `.agent-workflow/project.yaml` |

